Pe dată de 2011-01-27 05:03, Dasein a scris:
> OK I’m a bit of a Nethack noob, only recently started playing, haven’t
> made it much further than Sokoban / Minetown so far. But I’ve had some
> good luck with gear for a barbarian I’ve started, and wanted a bit of
> advice to try and avoid doing something stupid.
> Very early on (D lvl 2 I think?) I found an armour shop, and my dog
> grabbed for me boots and gloves, which turned out to be +3 boots, and
> gauntlets of power. Rock on. On D lvl 3 or so I found an aligned
> altar, though have had bad luck so far with corpses. I’m currently on
> D lvl 5, I’m exp lvl 4. My dog got separated from me and killed by
> something  But I figure it’s not a huge deal, since with STR 25 and a
> battle-axe and AC 3 I’m killing things effortlessly, and I can use the
> altar to BUC test stuff.
Sounds good!  I haven't really played a barbarian so far, so my advice
is fairly general.  With an altar probably close to the mine entry, it
certainly pays to check out the higher mine levels for some more good
armor, and maybe a stack of daggers.  A dwarfish mithril coat could make
your early game much safer.

> So what’s the best plan now? From what I gather the usual plan is
> Sokoban, then mines down to mine’s end, then back to main dungeon
> branch. But I’m thinking of taking a quick trip into the mines, since
> I should be able to handle very easily the monsters there, and can
> quickly get a bunch of XP, gold and gems (got to watch out for traps
> though). Is this a good plan?
Sounds reasonable to me.  If I don't have other convincing arguments, I
usually descend into the main dungeon until level 5 or so, then explore
the mines until mine town, then do Sokoban (and the dungeon levels
in-between, of course), and afterwards return for mine's end.  I
wouldn't go deeper than mine town without at least decent magic
cancellation, if I were relying on melee combat and physical strength only.

> Is it worth hanging around the higher D
> levels and trying to collect corpses to sac at the altar?
Depends on what you want to do.  At a level with an altar, you can
basically stay as long as you want (sacrificing everything that is safe,
and praying when you get weak).  Probably a good strategy is to do that
until you get your Cleaver.

> Is it worth
> trying to skill up other weapons to allow for more weapon diversity or
> just stick to axe and hope for Cleaver?
For other weapons, I'd probably wish for Mjollnir once I'd get the
chance (provided that not more than a single artifact has appeared so
far), but normal war hammers to train with are a bit hard to find.  A
stack of daggers is usually handy for ranged combat (especially if you
can enchant them once you have enough), but a barbarian can't reach more
than basic skill here.

> Is getting another pet a priority or not?
> Any advice appreciated!
Depends.  If I am strong enough and have other options of dealing with
(or getting away from) real trouble, I prefer to go without a pet for
levelling up faster (thereby increasing max HPs).  The downside is that
the monsters I meet will also be stronger as my XL increases.

